      "id": "NOC-01",
      "chapter": "global",
      "anchor": "global-near-one-type",
      "title": "The cost of near terms with prescribed flag ranks",
      "statement": "Only points with least size below one half can contribute nonidentity near terms. For a fixed ordered list of positive jumps j with total J≤q and length a, their integral on the moderate region is at most 2Mκⱼ∏ᵢ[2fjᵢ log(1/(2τ∗))], hence at most 2MκⱼYᵃ for Y=22fq² log X.",
      "hypotheses": "Self-dual unitary lattice in signature (p,q), q≥1, the scale and spectral gap hypotheses of the discrete series count, the near-unipotence and pointwise kernel bounds, the lattice count for a fixed flag and the normalized flag measure inequality.",
